      "writtenOn": "2019-07-04T00:49:42Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Moving delay from default parameter to every call site does not make much difference.\n\nWhy is this delay needed?\n\nNormally this should not wait at all, what should happen is that the command is sent to the wirite() method, and then the read() should be scanned to see the command echoed, then all output \\n\u0027prompt\u0027 dropped.\n\nthis guarantees that the command was executed and does not waste any time.\n\n\nfor some commands you would care about their output, in that case you might watch for the command echo and then collect the output til the next prompts shows up.\n\nThis would make the system more robust, now your are waiting for LF and consider it the end of the command, it won\u0027t be necessary if the test makes sure that it gets the expected echo after the command is entered.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 139,
        "startChar": 5,
        "endLine": 140,
        "endChar": 25
      },
